    {
      "title": "US House Republicans quash effort to impeach Defence Secretary Hegseth",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-house-republicans-quash-effort-to-impeach-defence-secretary-hegseth-126111100060_1.html",
      "description": "The House on Tuesday turned aside a resolution to impeach Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, halting an effort to remove the Pentagon chief for his conduct in office and his handling of the war in Iran.\nThe vote came as Republicans grapple with the fallout from sweeping midterm losses that some in the party have blamed on the war in Iran and the resulting surge in gas prices. But after President Donald Trump signalled strong support for Hegseth, GOP lawmakers largely stood by the secretary on Tuesday. They rejected the impeachment effort led by Kentucky Republican Thomas Massie and backed by Democrats.\nThe vote may only delay an impeachment push against Hegseth, with Democrats set to take control of the House and Senate in January.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-11T02:43:03"
    }
